      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186105903-draft/plots/40fd34d7027860f81b62c6ba19c4cc81b829739efe27baaee7ff13a7e1dd5778.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC.$ Round your answer to two decimal places.",
        ":question/requires-calculator": true,
        ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=3, \\\\ b & =AC=7, \\\\ m∠A & ={128}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{128}^{∘}=0.788\\,011,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{128}^{∘} \\\\  & =10.5\\cdot (0.788\\,011) \\\\  & ≈8.27,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/id": "46c7d550-5539-5147-a1c3-2ca1039d03b7",
