    "source_id": "q-279752",
    "record": {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186105903,
        "id": "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530",
        "title": "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186105903-draft/plots/af7775d01d42bb6755e49d46fbe1c4676a362e421b721c6b04380d57d4c2b813.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ above is{{field-1}}.",
        ":question/requires-calculator": true,
        ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=4, \\\\ a & =BC=8, \\\\ m∠B & ={40}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘}=0.642\\,788,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘} \\\\  & =16\\cdot (0.642\\,788) \\\\  & ≈10.3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest tenth**.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/id": "20f725d1-f0da-59df-9720-ff98112996a8",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "0e4b2892-4b40-5a3b-a94a-249fc8803a48",
