      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186105903-draft/plots/4a0310e0932e1dd8fa71ad57cd47416eb0dff7d5c4b3731d63cafb0dc311e2ee.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}} ${\\text{ft}}^{2}.$",
        ":question/requires-calculator": true,
        ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=18, \\\\ b & =AC=12, \\\\ m∠A & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘}=0.866\\,025,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 18\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =108\\cdot (0.866\\,025…) \\\\  & ≈93.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest tenth**.",
